reply.analysis:
No scores are visible, and all nine trials trained without error, so I can't rank them. Several ideas rest on the task's physics and stay near 1.0–1.2x compute, so they keep most of the step budget:
- footprint pooling, because the landing height is the maximum height under a brick's footprint and every covered cell must be missing;
- a global broadcast, for support and DONE decisions;
- a per-column MLP stem, for each column's build height relative to the target layers;
- shared 3D convolutions across layers.

Costs above 1.5x lose steps. Because this is the last round, I combine pieces that fit the task and keep each cost low, so the final top-3 has strong, varied candidates:
- column stem with the footprint head;
- voxel encoder with the footprint head;
- a learned footprint-shaped convolution added to the fixed max, min and mean pooling.

Each candidate keeps the global broadcast and stays at about 1.1–1.4x the starting compute.
